Fresh Claude Code session: IMPLEMENTATION.

Inputs:
- User prompt: {{run.dir}}/prompt/prompt.md
- Design: {{run.dir}}/design/design.md
- Issues from prior attempts: {{run.issues-file}}
- Latest periodic supervisor direction, when present: {{run.dir}}/supervision/current.md
- Original repository root: {{inputs.repo-root}}
- Worktree: {{run.worktree-dir}}

The current working directory is the isolated worktree. Make changes there.

Goal:
Implement the design and resolve all outstanding issues.

Before editing, check whether the supervisor direction file exists. When it is
present, read it alongside the exact reports it cites, follow its validated
prefix and revised strategy, and explain any evidence-backed departure in the
implementation summary. Do not treat stale generic issues as stronger evidence
than a newer exact gate report.

Testing policy (deterministic-first — this workflow's core rule):
- Testing is NOT your job. Do NOT run tests, lint, type checks, builds, or
  `npm`/`bb` commands. Do not invoke any test runner.
- Two deterministic test gates run AFTER this node — `bb test` (cheap smoke
  suite) then the Playwright browser suite — and their failures come back to
  you as `issues.json` entries on the next attempt. You will be re-entered
  with those issues if a gate fails.
- Your `status.json` `"pass"` only means "implementation complete and ready
  for the deterministic gates" — NEVER "tests passed". Do not claim a gate's
  result; the gates speak for themselves.

Rules:
- You may edit source code and tests (the test files themselves), but do not
  execute them.
- Keep changes focused on the prompt and design.
- Do not push or create a pull request.
- Do not edit this workflow or its run artifacts.
- Commit coherent changes locally when the repository uses Git.
- If the change alters a Tesseraft capability, update `STATUS.edn`; leave
  `bb status`/regeneration to the deterministic gates or a later authoring
  surface — do not run it here.
- Fail only when actionable work remains; write clear issues for the next
  implementation attempt.

Write:
- Summary: {{run.dir}}/execution/summary-{{run.round}}.md
- Status: {{run.dir}}/execution/status-{{run.round}}.json
- If failing: {{run.dir}}/execution/issues-{{run.round}}.json

Status examples:
{"status":"pass","summary":"implementation complete; deterministic gates pending","issues_file":null}
{"status":"fail","summary":"implementation needs another attempt","issues_file":"execution/issues-{{run.round}}.json"}